WEBVTT

00:00:00.630 --> 00:00:02.910
A robot shouldn't need a new training run

00:00:02.910 --> 00:00:04.800
for every new household task.

00:00:05.070 --> 00:00:08.470
What if teaching it were as natural as showing it what you mean?

00:00:09.216 --> 00:00:11.856
That is the promise of in-context learning.

00:00:11.976 --> 00:00:14.076
Pretraining builds capability;

00:00:14.196 --> 00:00:17.966
demonstrations, instructions, and feedback guide it at deployment,

00:00:18.096 --> 00:00:19.936
with the model's weights fixed.

00:00:20.663 --> 00:00:23.583
This survey, In-Context Learning for Robots,

00:00:23.783 --> 00:00:25.783
maps a path from reusable skills

00:00:25.883 --> 00:00:28.323
to robots that can be taught in the world.

00:00:28.940 --> 00:00:30.500
The vision reaches further:

00:00:30.620 --> 00:00:32.920
carry what is taught into new situations,

00:00:33.140 --> 00:00:34.840
compose unfamiliar tasks,

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:37.690
and ultimately improve how robots learn.

00:00:37.880 --> 00:00:39.480
Robots that learn what you need,

00:00:39.560 --> 00:00:40.700
where you need them.
